{"title":"Volition Street Smart Tour: One Toronto Lot. Four Homes. Four OWNERS.","startsAt":"2026-10-17T13:00:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-17T15:00:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"### **Tour a Real-World Toronto Condominiumization Project**\n\nWhat if, instead of building a multiplex and renting out the units, you could **build multiple homes on a single Toronto lot and sell each one individually?**\n\nThat's the idea behind **condominiumization** – what we're calling the \"Missing Middle 2.0\" investment strategy – and for this Meetup, we're going to walk through a real project that's actually doing it.\n\nWhen most people hear the word \"condo,\" they probably picture one of two things: **a box in the sky, or a unit in a large stacked townhouse development.**\n\nThis is neither.\n\nWhat if you could create a \"condo\" that **looks and feels much more like a traditional home**? One with its own front door, multiple floors and the privacy and feel of a house – nestled discreetly into an established residential neighbourhood rather than looking like an obvious townhouse development?\n\n**That's what Harvie is creating.**\n\nThe Harvie project started with a single-family property. Today, it's being transformed into **three townhouse-style homes plus a garden suite**, each designed to be separately titled and sold individually.\n\nMost missing-middle investment strategies (like the well-known \"4+1\") follow essentially the same playbook:\n**Buy a property. Add units. Rent them out. Hold.**\n\nHarvie asks a different question:\n**What if the target customer wasn't four tenants... but four HOMEOWNERS?**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n### **A Different Kind of Missing Middle**\n\nWe've spent a lot of time at Volition talking about Toronto's changing housing rules and the opportunities they create for small investors and developers. But almost all of that conversation has focused on **creating more rental housing**.\n\nCondominiumization introduces another possibility:\n**Creating more ownership housing.**\n\nFor many aspiring homeowners, there's a gap between the two traditional choices.\n\nOn one side is the **traditional house** – your own front door, multiple floors, privacy and the experience of living in an established residential neighbourhood – but increasingly at a price many aspiring homeowners simply can't afford.\n\nOn the other is the more attainable **condo apartment or stacked townhouse** – which may fit the budget better, but may not deliver the kind of home or lifestyle they're actually aspiring to own.\n\n**But what if there were something in between?**\n\nA home with its own front door. Multiple floors. More privacy. A residential streetscape. A home that feels like a real home, in a real neighbourhood – but on a smaller footprint and potentially at a more attainable price point than a traditional detached or semi-detached house.\n\n**That's the homebuyer Harvie is designed for.**\n\nWe're not just talking about adding density. We're talking about potentially creating **a type of ownership housing that sits between the condo apartment and the traditional Toronto house.**\n\nThat's what makes this \"Missing Middle 2.0\" concept so interesting.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n### **From One Single-Family Property to Four Individually Owned Homes**\n\nThe concept sounds simple:\n**Take one Toronto residential property. Redevelop it into multiple family-sized homes. Condominiumize the property. Sell each home separately.**\n\nBut here's the critical difference:\n**You can't simply design the same rental multiplex you would have built for four tenants and decide afterward that you're going to sell the units individually.**\n\n**The end product has to be something a homeowner actually wants to BUY.**\n\nDifferent customer. Different product. Different design. Different economics.\n\nThat changes everything from the site you choose and the layout of the building to privacy, sound separation, construction quality, materials, finishes and how the individual homes actually function day-to-day.\n\nAnd rather than explain all of that with slides in a conference room:\n**We're taking you directly inside the Harvie project.**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n### **What We'll Explore**\n\nUsing Harvie as our real-world case study, we'll dig into the questions that actually matter if you're considering this strategy:\n\n* **How does condominiumization actually work?** How do you go from one Toronto property to multiple separately titled homes that can ultimately be sold to individual homeowners?\n* **What makes a property a good candidate?** We'll look at how site dimensions, neighbourhood, comparable sales, acquisition costs and the potential value of the finished homes factor into choosing the right project.\n* **What do you build when your customer is a HOMEOWNER instead of a tenant?** We'll explore the design decisions behind Harvie's vertical townhouse-style homes, including layouts, privacy, sound separation, utilities and the details that make a unit actually feel like a home.\n* **What does it take to get a project like this approved and built?** We'll unpack some of the municipal, planning, design and construction challenges encountered along the way – while seeing the actual materials, construction methods and finished product firsthand.\n* **Does the business model actually work?** We'll explore the economics, financing and exit strategy, and how developing homes for individual sale changes the equation compared with building and holding a conventional rental multiplex.\n* And perhaps most importantly, **what do you only learn by actually doing it?** We'll get into the real-world challenges, surprises and lessons from executing the strategy – including what might be done differently on the next project.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n### **Hear Directly From the Developer Behind Harvie**\n\nOur expert guest speaker **Daniel Zimberoff** is the investor and developer behind Harvie. He'll take us through the actual project firsthand – why it was designed this way, how the strategy was executed, what happened along the way and what he's learned from bringing it to reality.\n\nDan also runs a consulting practice **teaching other investors and developers how to execute condominiumization projects of their own.**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n### **Come See the Real Thing**\n\nThis isn't a hypothetical pro forma.\nIt isn't a rendering.\nAnd it isn't a seminar about what *might* be possible.\n\n**We're going to walk through the real thing.**\n\n**One Toronto lot. Four homes. Four OWNERS.**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\n\n***\n\n**Schedule:**\nSaturday, October 17, 2026, 1:00-3:00 pm\n\n**Location:**\n534 Harvie Ave, Toronto, ON\n*(Limited street parking available. A short walk from the Eglinton Crosstown LRT - Fairbank and Caledonia stations)*\n\n***\n\n**Volition Properties:**\n\n*Make smarter real estate moves — buy, sell, or invest with confidence. Volition Properties offers tailored advice, education, and community — grounded in strategy, built on trust.*\n\nContact us today for any questions about real estate in Toronto!\n📧 info@volitionprop.com\n🌐 [www.volitionprop.com](https://www.volitionprop.com \"https://www.volitionprop.com\")\n📞 1-877-416-BRRR","venue":{"name":"534 Harvie Avenue","address":"534 Harvie Ave, York, ON M6E 4M1, Canada, Toronto","lat":43.691097,"lng":-79.45616,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"✪ TORONTO REAL ESTATE INVESTOR MASTERMIND ✪","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/3/e/a/highres_536398346.jpeg"}